From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Gardner <jamestexasgardner@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] libkrun: add krun_add_virtiofs_backend for Rust embedders

Expose the DynFileSystem backend through the library: a Rust program
that links the `libkrun` crate (crate-type "lib") can attach a virtio-fs
device whose FUSE requests are answered by an object in its own
process.

    pub fn krun_add_virtiofs_backend(
        ctx_id: u32,
        tag: &str,
        shm_size: u64,
        backend: Arc<dyn DynFileSystem>,
    ) -> i32

`shm_size` is the DAX window size in bytes; 0 attaches the device
without one. It returns KRUN_SUCCESS or -ENOENT for an unknown context,
like krun_add_virtiofs*.

FsDeviceConfig gains `custom_backend`; when it is set, the builder hands
the backend to the device and `shared_dir` is unused. Every existing
constructor sets it to None, so the C API is unchanged.

The crate re-exports `devices::virtio::fs` as `virtio_fs` and
`linux_error` so an embedder can name the trait and its request types
without depending on krun-devices directly.

This is a Rust-only entry point: a trait object does not cross the C
ABI. A C embedder would need a callback table; that is left for a
follow-up if there is demand.

Signed-off-by: James Gardner <jamestexasgardner@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: jamestexas <18285880+jamestexas@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/libkrun/src/lib.rs       | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/vmm/src/builder.rs       |  4 ++++
 src/vmm/src/vmm_config/fs.rs |  3 +++
 3 files changed, 46 insertions(+)

